arguments.prompt:
You are building a Blazor Web App for a university course catalog. The project has already been scaffolded at `/tmp/sv-62c31a795c78465d845b58741fb96c23/CourseCatalog` using `dotnet new blazor -int None` (Static SSR, no interactivity).

## Key Architecture Rules (Static SSR)
- Do NOT add `@rendermode` to any component
- Forms use standard HTML POST with `[SupplyParameterFromForm]` and require `<AntiforgeryToken />`
- No `@onclick` or event handlers — use form submissions and links
- No `IJSRuntime`
- Query string parameters use `[SupplyParameterFromQuery]`
- Components can inject services directly (no API layer needed)

## Requirements
1. **Homepage** — featured courses and department links
2. **Browse courses** — searchable, filterable list (by department, search term)
3. **Course detail page** — description, schedule, credits, instructor bio
4. **Enrollment request form** — name, student ID, course selection (standard HTML form POST)
5. No authentication
6. Intranet deployment, fast connectivity

## What to Build

### 1. Data Model & Service (`Models/` and `Services/`)

Create `Models/Department.cs`:
```csharp
namespace CourseCatalog.Models;

public class Department
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string Name { get; set; } = "";
    public string Code { get; set; } = "";
    public string Description { get; set; } = "";
}
```

Create `Models/Course.cs`:
```csharp
namespace CourseCatalog.Models;

public class Course
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string Title { get; set; } = "";
    public string Code { get; set; } = "";
    public string Description { get; set; } = "";
    public int Credits { get; set; }
    public string Schedule { get; set; } = "";
    public string InstructorName { get; set; } = "";
    public string InstructorBio { get; set; } = "";
    public int DepartmentId { get; set; }
    public string DepartmentName { get; set; } = "";
    public bool IsFeatured { get; set; }
}
```

Create `Models/EnrollmentRequest.cs`:
```csharp
using System.ComponentModel.DataAnnotations;

namespace CourseCatalog.Models;

public class EnrollmentRequest
{
    [Required(ErrorMessage = "Name is required.")]
    public string StudentName { get; set; } = "";

    [Required(ErrorMessage = "Student ID is required.")]
    public string StudentId { get; set; } = "";

    [Required(ErrorMessage = "Please select a course.")]
    [Range(1, int.MaxValue, ErrorMessage = "Please select a course.")]
    public int CourseId { get; set; }
}
```

Create `Services/ICatalogService.cs`:
```csharp
using CourseCatalog.Models;

namespace CourseCatalog.Services;

public interface ICatalogService
{
    List<Department> GetDepartments();
    Department? GetDepartment(int id);
    List<Course> GetCourses(string? searchTerm = null, int? departmentId = null);
    List<Course> GetFeaturedCourses();
    Course? GetCourse(int id);
    bool SubmitEnrollmentRequest(EnrollmentRequest request);
}
```

Create `Services/CatalogService.cs` — an in-memory implementation with seed data:
